  Untranslated regions derived from NCBI RefSeq
  --------------------------------------------
  Records in `inputs/utrs/utrs.fasta` extracted from RefSeq entries
  NM_000518.5 (HBB), NM_000558.5 (HBA1), NM_000414.4 (HSD17B4) and NM_002795.3
  (PSMB3), retrieved by NCBI efetch on 2026-10-19 and cut to the span each
  record's own CDS feature annotates.

    NCBI "places no restrictions on the use or distribution of the data
    contained therein", while noting that a submitter or country of origin may
    claim rights in all or part of a submission, and that NCBI cannot give
    unrestricted permission on their behalf.
    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/

  Untranslated regions read from patent and regulatory documents
  -------------------------------------------------------------
  The remaining records in `inputs/utrs/utrs.fasta` were extracted from
  published documents rather than from a sequence database: a CureVac patent
  sequence listing (US 11,241,493 B2, SEQ ID NO: 148, corroborated against
  US 2022/0233568 A1) and a GSRS record for BNT162b2. Patent specifications and
  their sequence listings are published public documents. `inputs/utrs/PROVENANCE.md`
  states, per record, whether its span is stated by the source or produced by
  arithmetic, and which boundaries rest on secondary sources.

  Predicted structure from the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
  inputs/structures/AF-P15421-F1-model_v6.pdb is the AlphaFold DB model of
  UniProtKB P15421 (GLPE_HUMAN), byte-unmodified; its header carries the
  database's own citation and terms.

    Jumper, J. et al. Highly accurate protein structure prediction with
    AlphaFold. Nature 596, 583-589 (2021). doi:10.1038/s41586-021-03819-2.
    Varadi, M. et al. AlphaFold Protein Structure Database. Nucleic Acids
    Research (2022). AlphaFold DB data are available under the Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) License. https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/

  Other sequences
  ---------------
  The remaining six of the 85: the five Cas orthologs in `inputs/prt/`
  (PRT-03 to PRT-07) and `inputs/e3/eGFP.fasta`, an engineered variant of
  Aequorea victoria GFP at 239 residues. Their origin is not recorded in this
  repository beyond the provenance notes under `inputs/`, so this notice makes
  no claim over them and asserts no terms on anyone's behalf. Anyone
  redistributing them should establish their provenance first.

The deposits themselves are not in this repository. They are the recorded
results of runs described in `pins/*-PROVENANCE.md`, built by this project. A deposit that embeds a
third-party input embeds it under that input's terms, as named here.

The algorithms this analysis measures are described in the published
literature, and the references in README.md are scholarly debts rather than
licence conditions.
